      "caveat": "IM-GBM-28: 4 samples in collection order, placed by the day each was collected (days from diagnosis, from the study's timeline). 8 mutations; 8 are drawn. VAF is variant reads ÷ (variant + reference reads) in each sample. A mutation called in one sample is followed into the others: there it is an uncalled mutation where the study's uncalled-mutations profile found variant reads (drawn with that VAF), not found (VAF 0) where the sample was sequenced for the gene, or NOT PROFILED where the sample's panel does not cover the gene — never 0. A line joins a mutation's VAFs from the first to the last sample with variant reads, as the portal draws it; it bridges a not-profiled sample, or one called without allele counts, with a dashed segment. Fusions recorded as mutations are left out, as the portal leaves them out. The patient list holds the cohort's patients with two or more samples and a mutation with allele counts: 36 patients. Sorted with the most samples first, then by patient id across the cohort; every page is a slice of that one order, and the download holds every row kept, with every column. ",
      "method": {
        "steps": [
          {
            "kind": "fetch",
            "title": "Count the patients per cohort and study",
            "detail": "The evolution:counts query above: every patient of each cohort with two or more samples and at least one called mutation with allele counts (variant reads above zero, and reference reads), with their sample count, called mutations and those with allele counts.",
            "params": [
              [
                "Glioma · glioma_msk_2018",
                "36"
              ]
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "fetch",
            "title": "Sort them together and take one page",
            "detail": "The evolution:rows query above: the patients of every cohort and study combined in one query, sorted most samples first, then by patient id, and the 25 rows of the first page taken. Every other page, and the download, is the same query at another offset."
          },
          {
            "kind": "fetch",
            "title": "Read IM-GBM-28's samples and mutations",
            "detail": "The patient's samples (evolution:samples, with the gene panel each was sequenced with for mutations) and timeline (for each sample's collection day), numbered in collection order; then evolution:mutations: every mutation called in any of the patient's samples (fusions left out), merged across samples by gene, protein change and genomic position as the portal merges them, with its state in every sample — called (VAF = variant reads ÷ (variant + reference reads)), called without allele counts, uncalled with variant reads (the study's uncalled-mutations profile; drawn with its VAF), not found in a sample sequenced for the gene (VAF 0), or not profiled (the sample's panel omits the gene, or it was not sequenced for mutations: no VAF). The figure draws every mutation the table's query keeps that has a VAF in some sample where it was called.",
            "params": [
              [
